    "['remote-mep ccm-receive enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 mep 32 remote-mep 31 ccm-enable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `remote-mep ccm-receive enable`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 mep 32 remote-mep 31 ccm-enable\\n##\\n\\nThis command:\\n1. Sets up CCM (Continuity Check Message) reception for the remote MEP\\n2. Maintains the same maintenance domain (md1) and association (ma1)\\n3. Follows Juniper's hierarchical configuration style\\n4. Uses MEP ID 32 (local) and remote MEP ID 31 to match the original configuration context\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 mep 32 remote-mep 31 ccm-enable'}]]": 1,
    "['ais enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 ais enable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper command for `ais enable` in the context of CFM (Connectivity Fault Management):\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 ais enable\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper implementation is structured differently than Huawei's, requiring the full OAM/CFM hierarchy path to enable AIS (Alarm Indication Signal). The command enables AIS transmission for the specified maintenance domain and association.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 ais enable'}]]": 1,
    "['ais link-status interface [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check interval 60', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI CFM AIS configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check interval 60\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 link-trace sender-id chassis\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 ais interface ge-1/0/2\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper\\'s implementation differs slightly:\\n1. The AIS function is enabled by simply associating it with an interface\\n2. The VLAN tagging and level are typically configured under the MA context\\n3. Juniper doesn\\'t require explicit \"link-status\" specification as it\\'s implied in the AIS interface binding', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check interval 60'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 link-trace sender-id chassis', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI CFM AIS configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 continuity-check interval 60\\n